= The Elements

Body text follows immediately, at the ordinary rhythm — a heading is never
the last thing on a page, and never alone.

== Composition

A section opens here, and from this point the running head at the top of
the page reads "Composition" until the next one changes it.

=== The measure

A subsection narrows the topic without opening a new run in the running
head.

==== Choosing a ratio

Fourth level: still sans, still bold, one size larger than the paragraph
beneath it.

===== On old-style figures

Fifth level: serif small caps at exactly the body size around it.

====== A closing remark

Sixth level: serif italic, the same size as the text it introduces.

